ction was_interrupted","tags":"","url":"proc/was_interrupted.html"},{"title":"setup_handler – FTDSS","text":"public  subroutine setup_handler() Sets up the signal handler to catch interrupt signals.\nThis should be called once at the beginning of the program to enable\ninterrupt detection. Arguments None Calls proc~~setup_handler~~CallsGraph proc~setup_handler setup_handler interface~c_setup_signal_handler c_setup_signal_handler proc~setup_handler->interface~c_setup_signal_handler Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine setup_handler () implicit none call c_setup_signal_handler () end subroutine setup_handler","tags":"","url":"proc/setup_handler.html"},{"title":"finalize_vtk_object – FTDSS","text":"private  subroutine finalize_vtk_object(self) Releases memory allocated by the C++ backend. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( type_vtk ), intent(inout) :: self The vtk object to be finalized. Calls proc~~finalize_vtk_object~~CallsGraph proc~finalize_vtk_object finalize_vtk_object interface~vtk_finalize vtk_finalize proc~finalize_vtk_object->interface~vtk_finalize interface~vtu_finalize vtu_finalize proc~finalize_vtk_object->interface~vtu_finalize Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine finalize_vtk_object ( self ) !> The vtk object to be finalized. type ( type_vtk ), intent ( inout ) :: self if ( c_associated ( self % handle )) then select case ( trim ( adjustl ( self % reader_type ))) case ( \"vtk\" ) call vtk_finalize ( self % handle ) case ( \"vtu\" ) call vtu_finalize ( self % handle ) case default ! Do nothing for unknown reader types. end select self % handle = c_null_ptr end if end subroutine finalize_vtk_object","tags":"","url":"proc/finalize_vtk_object.html"},{"title":"get_active_region_info – FTDSS","text":"interface Calls interface~~get_active_region_info~~CallsGraph interface~get_active_region_info type_vtk%get_active_region_info proc~get_active_region_info get_active_region_info interface~get_active_region_info->proc~get_active_region_info interface~type_vtk_cell_get_dimension type_vtk_cell%type_vtk_cell_get_dimension proc~get_active_region_info->interface~type_vtk_cell_get_dimension unique unique proc~get_active_region_info->unique proc~type_vtk_cell_get_dimension type_vtk_cell_get_dimension interface~type_vtk_cell_get_dimension->proc~type_vtk_cell_get_dimension Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls