ype Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine initialize_profiler ( self , labels ) implicit none class ( type_profiler ), intent ( inout ) :: self character ( len = 10 ), intent ( in ) :: labels (:) integer ( int32 ) :: i ! --- Profiler Sections Initialization --- if ( allocated ( self % sections )) deallocate ( self % sections ) if ( size ( labels ) > 0 ) then allocate ( self % sections ( size ( labels ))) do i = 1 , size ( labels ) self % sections ( i )% label = trim ( labels ( i )) self % sections ( i )% total_time = 0.0d0 self % sections ( i )% start_time = 0.0d0 self % sections ( i )% call_count = 0 end do end if end subroutine initialize_profiler","tags":"","url":"proc/initialize_profiler.html"},{"title":"record_profiler – FTDSS","text":"private  subroutine record_profiler(self, label) Type Bound type_profiler Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( type_profiler ), intent(inout) :: self integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: label Calls proc~~record_profiler~~CallsGraph proc~record_profiler type_profiler%record_profiler proc~get_time_record_string get_time_record_string proc~record_profiler->proc~get_time_record_string Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one 