n ), optional :: millisecond !> Timezone offset in minutes integer ( int32 ), intent ( in ), optional :: timezone_offset self % year = year self % month = month self % day = day self % hour = optval ( hour , 0 ) self % minute = optval ( minute , 0 ) self % second = optval ( second , 0 ) self % millisecond = optval ( millisecond , 0 ) self % timezone_offset = optval ( timezone_offset , 0 ) end subroutine set_datetime","tags":"","url":"proc/set_datetime.html"},{"title":"set_from_iso_string – FTDSS","text":"private  subroutine set_from_iso_string(self, iso_str, stat) Parses an ISO 8601 string and updates the object. Type Bound type_datetime Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( type_datetime ), intent(inout) :: self The type_datetime instance character(len=*), intent(in) :: iso_str ISO 8601 formatted string integer(kind=int32), intent(inout), optional :: stat Status flag (0: success, non-zero: error). Optional. Calls proc~~set_from_iso_string~~CallsGraph proc~set_from_iso_string type_datetime%set_from_iso_string proc~is_iso_string_datetime type_datetime%is_iso_string_datetime proc~set_from_iso_string->proc~is_iso_string_datetime Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~set_from_iso_string~~CalledByGraph proc~set_from_iso_string type_datetime%set_from_iso_string none~set~10 type_datetime%set none~set~10->proc~set_from_iso_string proc~initialize_meteorology_data type_meteorology_data%initialize_meteorology_data proc~initialize_meteorology_data->none~set~10 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine set_from_iso_string ( self , iso_str , stat ) implicit none !> The type_datetime instance class ( type_datetime ), intent ( inout ) :: self !> ISO 8601 formatted string character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: iso_str !> Status flag (0: success, non-zero: error). Optional. integer ( int32 ), intent ( inout ), optional :: stat integer ( int32 ) :: length , ios , tzh , tzm character ( len = 1 ) :: sig if ( present ( stat )) stat = 0 length = len_trim ( iso_str ) ! 1. Validate format if (. not . self % is_iso ( iso_str )) then if ( present ( stat )) stat = - 1 return end if ! 2. Reset defaults self % hour = 0 self % minute = 0 self % second = 0 self % millisecond = 0 self % timezone_offset = 0 ! 3. Parse components based on string length ! Date: YYYY-MM-DD read ( iso_str ( 1 : 10 ), '(i4, 1x, i2, 1x, i2)' , iostat = ios ) self % year , self % month , self % day if ( ios /= 0 ) then if ( present ( stat )) stat = ios return end if ! Time: hh:mm if ( length >= 16 ) then read ( iso_str ( 12 : 16 ), '(i2, 1x, i2)' , iostat = ios ) self % hour , self % minute if ( ios /= 0 ) then if ( present ( stat )) stat = ios return end if end if ! Seconds: ss if ( length >= 19 ) then read ( iso_str ( 18 : 19 ), '(i2)' , iostat = ios ) self % second if ( ios /= 0 ) then if ( present ( stat )) stat = ios return end if end if ! Timezone Offset: Z or +/-HH:MM if ( index ( iso_str , 'Z' ) > 0 ) then self % timezone_offset = 0 else if ( length >= 25 ) then read ( iso_str ( 20 : 25 ), '(a1, i2, 1x, i2)' , iostat = ios ) sig , tzh , tzm if ( ios == 0 ) then self % timezone_offset = tzh * 60 + tzm if ( sig == '-' ) self % timezone_offset = - self % timezone_offset else if ( present ( stat )) stat = ios return end if end if end subroutine set_from_iso_string","tags":"","url":"proc/set_from_iso_string.html"},{"title":"set_now_datetime – FTDSS","text":"private  subroutine set_now_datetime(self) Sets components using the system clock. Type Bound type_datetime Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( type_datetime ), intent(inout) :: self The type_datetime instance Called by proc~~set_now_datetime~~CalledByGraph proc~set_now_datetime type_datetime%set_now_datetime none~set~10 type_datetime%set none~set~10->proc~set_now_datetime proc~initialize_meteorology_data type_meteorology_data%initialize_meteorology_data proc~initialize_meteorology_data->none~set~10 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine set_now_datetime ( self ) implicit none !> The type_datetime i