ction Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine get_dt ( self , dt , time_unit ) implicit none class ( type_time ), intent ( in ) :: self !> Output time step real ( real64 ), intent ( inout ) :: dt !> Target time unit (optional) type ( type_constant_value ), intent ( in ), optional :: time_unit real ( real64 ) :: coeff if ( present ( time_unit )) then coeff = 1.0d0 / time_unit % value else coeff = 1.0d0 end if dt = self % dt_s * coeff end subroutine get_dt","tags":"","url":"proc/get_dt.html"},{"title":"get_end_time – FTDSS","text":"private pure subroutine get_end_time(self, end_time) Type Bound type_time Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( type_time ), intent(in) :: self real(kind=real64), intent(inout) :: end_time Called by proc~~get_end_time~~CalledByGraph proc~get_end_time type_time%get_end_time proc~update_controls type_controls%update_controls proc~update_controls->proc~get_end_time proc~run_ftdss run_ftdss proc~run_ftdss->proc~update_controls interface~run_ftdss type_ftdss%run_ftdss interface~run_ftdss->proc~run_ftdss Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure subroutine get_end_time ( self , end_time ) implicit none class ( type_time ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( real64 ), intent ( inout ) :: end_time end_time = self % end_time end subroutine get_end_time","tags":"","url":"proc/get_end_time.html"},{"title":"get_time – FTDSS","text":"private  subroutine get_time(self, current_time, time_unit) Get current simulation time (seconds) with optional unit conversion.\nIf a target time unit is provided, the current_time is converted accordingly. Type Bound type_time Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( type_time ), intent(in) :: self real(kind=real64), intent(inout) :: current_time Output current time type( type_constant_value ), intent(in), optional :: time_unit Target time unit (optional) Called by proc~~get_time~~CalledByGraph proc~get_time type_time%get_time proc~apply_bc_ftdss apply_bc_ftdss proc~apply_bc_ftdss->proc~get_time proc~initialize_type_controls type_controls%initialize_type_controls proc~initialize_type_controls->proc~get_time proc~output_fields_ftdss output_fields_ftdss proc~output_fields_ftdss->proc~get_time proc~output_history_ftdss output_history_ftdss proc~output_history_ftdss->proc~get_time proc~update_controls type_controls%update_controls proc~update_controls->proc~get_time interface~apply_bc_ftdss type_ftdss%apply_bc_ftdss interface~apply_bc_ftdss->proc~apply_bc_ftdss interface~output_fields_ftdss type_ftdss%output_fields_ftdss interface~output_fields_ftdss->proc~output_fields_ftdss interface~output_history_ftdss type_ftdss%output_history_ftdss interface~output_history_ftdss->proc~output_history_ftdss proc~run_ftdss run_ftdss proc~run_ftdss->proc~update_controls proc~run_ftdss->interface~output_fields_ftdss proc~run_ftdss->interface~output_history_ftdss interface~solve_time_step_ftdss type_ftdss%solve_time_step_ftdss proc~run_ftdss->interface~solve_time_step_ftdss interface~run_ftdss type_ftdss%run_ftdss interface~run_ftdss->proc~run_ftdss proc~initialize_type_ftdss initialize_type_ftdss proc~initialize_type_ftdss->interface~apply_bc_ftdss proc~initialize_type_ftdss->interface~output_fields_ftdss proc~initialize_type_ftdss->interface~output_history_ftdss proc~solve_time_step_ftdss solve_time_step_ftdss proc~solve_time_step_ftdss->interface~apply_bc_ftdss interface~initialize_type_ftdss type_ftdss%initialize_type_ftdss interface~initialize_type_ftdss->proc~initialize_type_ftdss interface~solve_time_step_ftdss->proc~solve_time_step_ftdss Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine get_time ( self , current_time , time_unit ) implicit none class ( type_time ), intent ( in ) :: self !> Output current time real ( real64 ), intent ( inout ) :: current_time !> Target time unit (optional) type ( type_constant_value ), intent ( in ), optional :: time_unit real ( real64 ) :: coeff if ( present ( time_unit )) then coeff = 1.0d0 / time_unit % value else coeff = 1.0d0 end if current_time = self % current_time_s * coeff end subroutine get_time","tags":"","url":"proc/get_time.html"},{"title":"initialize_type_time – FTDSS","text":"private  subroutine initialize_type_time(self, input) Initialize the time control object using input configuration. Type Bound type_time Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( type_time ), intent(inout) :: self type( type_input ), intent(in) :: input Calls proc~~initialize_type_time~~CallsGraph proc~initialize_type_time type_time%initialize_type_time proc~compute_bdf_coefficients type_time%compute_bdf_coefficients proc~initialize_type_time->proc~compute_bdf_coefficients proc~initialize_type_ats type_ats%initialize_type_ats proc~initialize_type_time->proc~initialize_type_ats to_object to_object proc~initialize_type_time->to_object Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~initialize_type_time~~CalledByGraph proc~initialize_type_time type_time%initialize_type_time proc~initialize_type_controls type_controls%initialize_type_controls proc~initialize_type_controls->proc~initialize_type_time Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine initialize_type_time ( self , input ) implicit none class ( type_time ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( type_input ), intent ( in ) :: input integer ( int32 ) :: istat real ( real64 ) :: time_conv_coeff type ( type_constant_value ) :: time_unit ! --- BDF Settings --- self % target_bdf_order = input % basic % solver_settings % bdf_order if ( self % target_bdf_order > MAX_BDF_ORDER ) then self % target_bdf_order = MAX_BDF_ORDER end if self % current_bdf_order = 1 associate ( time_control => input % conditions % time_control ) ! --- 1. dt 関連の単位変換 (time_stepping%unit を使用) --- time_unit = TIME_UNITS % to_object ( time_control % time_stepping % unit ) time_conv_coeff = time_unit % value self % dt_s = time_control % time_stepping % initial_step * time_conv_coeff self % dt_s_max = time_control % time_stepping % max_step * time_conv_coeff self % dt_s_min = time_control % time_stepping % min_step * time_conv_coeff ! --- Allocate History --- if ( allocated ( self % dt_s_history )) deallocate ( self % dt_s_history ) allocate ( self % dt_s_history ( self % target_bdf_order ), stat = istat ) if ( istat == 0 ) then self % dt_s_history (:) = 0.0d0 self % dt_s_history ( 1 ) = self % dt_s end if ! --- Compute Initial Coefficients --- call self % compute_bdf_coefficients () ! --- 2. シミュレーション期間の単位変換 (simulation_period%unit を使用) --- ! 出力設定に関わらず，期間は simulation_period%unit に基づいて初期化する time_unit = TIME_UNITS % to_object ( time_control % simulation_period % unit ) self % start_time = time_control % simulation_period % start * time_unit % value self % end_time = time_control % simulation_period % end * time_unit % value self % current_time_s = self % start_time ! --- 3. ATS の初期化を追加 --- call self % ats % initialize ( input , self % dt_s_min , self % dt_s_max ) end associate end subroutine initialize_type_time","tags":"","url":"proc/initialize_type_time.html"},{"title":"set_dt – FTDSS","text":"private  subroutine set_dt(self, new_dt, time_unit) Set current time step size (seconds) with optional unit conversion.\nIf a target time unit is provided, dt is converted accordingly before setting. Type Bound type_time Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( type_time ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: new_dt Input time step type( type_constant_value ), intent(in), optional :: time_unit Target time unit (optional) Calls proc~~set_dt~~CallsGraph proc~set_dt type_time%set_dt proc~compute_bdf_coefficients type_time%compute_bdf_coefficients proc~set_dt->proc~compute_bdf_coefficients Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine set_dt ( self , new_dt , time_unit ) implicit none class ( type_time ), intent ( inout ) :: self !> Input time step real ( real64 ), intent ( in ) :: new_dt !> Target time unit (optional) type ( type_constant_value ), intent ( in ), optional :: time_unit real ( real64 ) :: dt if ( present ( time_unit )) then dt = new_dt * time_unit % value else dt = new_dt end if if ( dt <= self % dt_s_min ) then self % dt_s = self % dt_s_min else if ( dt >= self % dt_s_max ) then self % dt_s = self % dt_s_max else self % dt_s = dt end if call self % compute_bdf_coefficients () end subroutine set_dt","tags":"","url":"proc/set_dt.html"},{"title":"shift_time – FTDSS","text":"private  subroutine shift_time(self) Shift time history and update current time state after a successful step.\nAlso manages the ramping up of BDF order during initial steps. Type Bound type_time Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( type_time ), intent(inout) :: self Time control instance Calls proc~~shift_time~~CallsGraph proc~shift_time type_time%shift_time proc~compute_bdf_coefficients type_time%compute_bdf_coefficients proc~shift_time->proc~compute_bdf_coefficients Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~shift_time~~CalledByGraph proc~shift_time type_time%shift_time proc~update_type_time type_time%update_type_time proc~update_type_time->proc~shift_time proc~update_controls type_controls%update_controls proc~update_controls->proc~update_type_time proc~run_ftdss run_ftdss proc~run_ftdss->proc~update_controls interface~run_ftdss type_ftdss%run_ftdss interface~run_ftdss->proc~run_ftdss Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine shift_time ( self ) implicit none !> Time control instance class ( type_time ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer ( int32 ) :: n if (. not . allocated ( self % dt_s_history )) return n = size ( self % dt_s_history ) ! Update time self % time_old = self % current_time_s self % current_time_s = self % current_time_s + self % dt_s ! Shift history: dt_history(1) becomes current dt_n if ( n > 1 ) then self % dt_s_history ( 2 : n ) = self % dt_s_history ( 1 : n - 1 ) end if self % dt_s_history ( 1 ) = self % dt_s ! Update available BDF order (Ramp up strategy) if ( self % current_bdf_order < self % target_bdf_order ) then self % current_bdf_order = self % current_bdf_order + 1 end if ! Recompute coefficients call self % compute_bdf_coefficients () end subroutine shift_time","tags":"","url":"proc/shift_time.html"},{"title":"sync_with_output – FTDSS","text":"private  subroutine sync_with_output(self, next_output_time) Synchronize dt with the next output time. Type Bound type_time Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( type_time ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: next_output_time Called by proc~~sync_with_output~~CalledByGraph proc~sync_with_output type_time%sync_with_output proc~update_type_time type_time%update_type_time proc~update_type_time->proc~sync_with_output proc~update_controls type_controls%update_controls proc~update_controls->proc~update_type_time proc~run_ftdss run_ftdss proc~run_ftdss->proc~update_controls interface~run_ftdss type_ftdss%run_ftdss interface~run_ftdss->proc~run_ftdss Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine sync_with_output ( self , next_output_time ) implicit none class ( type_time ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( real64 ), intent ( in ) :: next_output_time real ( real64 ) :: time_to_output ! Remaining time until the next output. time_to_output = next_output_time - self % current_time_s ! If \"dt proposed by ATS\" is longer than \"remaining time\", ! shorten dt to align exactly with the output time. if ( self % dt_s > time_to_output . and . time_to_output > EPS_TIME ) then ! Note: exercise caution if remaining time is smaller than min_step. ! (Adjustment might have been insufficient in the previous step; decide to force alignment or error.) ! Determine policy: issue warning and force alignment, or ignore if too small. self % dt_s = time_to_output end if end subroutine sync_with_output","tags":"","url":"proc/sync_with_output.html"},{"title":"update_bdf_coefficients – FTDSS","text":"private  subroutine update_bdf_coefficients(self) Explicitly trigger an update of BDF coefficients. Type Bound type_time Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( type_time ), intent(inout) :: self Calls proc~~update_bdf_coefficients~~CallsGraph proc~update_bdf_coefficients type_time%update_bdf_coefficients proc~compute_bdf_coefficients type_time%c