rs to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code module subroutine calc_time_coefficient_bc ( self , current_time , coef , idx ) implicit none class ( abst_bc ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( real64 ), intent ( in ) :: current_time real ( real64 ), intent ( inout ) :: coef integer ( int32 ), intent ( inout ) :: idx integer ( int32 ) :: n , low , high , mid , hint , i integer ( int32 ), parameter :: MAX_LINEAR_STEPS = 4 logical :: found if (. not . allocated ( self % config % time_points )) then coef = 0.0d0 idx = 1 return end if n = size ( self % config % time_points ) if ( n < 2 . or . current_time <= self % config % time_points ( 1 )) then coef = 0.0d0 idx = 1 self % current_idx = 1 return end if if ( current_time >= self % config % time_points ( n )) then coef = 0.0d0 idx = n self % current_idx = n return end if ! ----- Hint-based local search (O(1) in typical forward-stepping) ----- found = . false . hint = self % current_idx if ( hint >= 1 . and . hint < n ) then ! Check current interval [hint, hint+1) if ( current_time >= self % config % time_points ( hint ) . and . & current_time < self % config % time_points ( hint + 1 )) then idx = hint found = . true . end if ! Forward linear search (normal time-stepping case) if (. not . found ) then do i = 1 , MAX_LINEAR_STEPS if ( hint + i >= n ) exit if ( current_time >= self % config % time_points ( hint + i ) . and . & current_time < self % config % time_points ( hint + i + 1 )) then idx = hint + i found = . true . exit end if end do end if ! Backward linear search (rollback case) if (. not . found ) then do i = 1 , MAX_LINEAR_STEPS if ( hint - i < 1 ) exit if ( current_time >= self % config % time_points ( hint - i ) . and . & current_time < self % config % time_points ( hint - i + 1 )) then idx = hint - i found = . true . exit end if end do end if end if ! ----- Fallback: Binary Search (O(log n)) ----- if (. not . found ) then low = 1 high = n do while ( high - low > 1 ) mid = ( low + high ) / 2 if ( current_time >= self % config % time_points ( mid )) then low = mid else high = mid end if end do idx = low end if ! Cache the found index for next call self % current_idx = idx ! Compute interpolation coefficient if ( self % config % time_points ( idx + 1 ) - self % config % time_points ( idx ) > epsilon ( 1.0d0 )) then coef = ( current_time - self % config % time_points ( idx )) / & ( self % config % time_points ( idx + 1 ) - self % config % time_points ( idx )) else coef = 0.0d0 end if end subroutine calc_time_coefficient_bc","tags":"","url":"proc/calc_time_coefficient_bc.html"},{"title":"calc_values_raw_bc – FTDSS","text":"module subroutine calc_values_raw_bc(self, current_time, out_values) Interface → Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( abst_bc ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: current_time real(kind=real64), intent(inout) :: out_values (:) Calls proc~~calc_values_raw_bc~~CallsGraph proc~calc_values_raw_bc calc_values_raw_bc interface~calc_time_coefficient_bc abst_bc%calc_time_coefficient_bc proc~calc_values_raw_bc->interface~calc_time_coefficient_bc proc~calc_time_coefficient_bc calc_time_coefficient_bc interface~calc_time_coefficient_bc->proc~calc_time_coefficient_bc Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~calc_values_raw_bc~~CalledByGraph proc~calc_values_raw_bc 